    "title": {
     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Meena asked 30 classmates their favourite game and wrote the answers in tally marks.\n\"Now I must organise them,\" she said."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "data",
     "tally mark",
     "frequency"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Data is a collection of facts, such as numbers or choices. We collect data by asking questions, observing or counting.\nWe organise data in a table using tally marks. Every fifth mark crosses the four before it. We then write the frequency, which is how many times each choice occurred.\nOrganised data is easy to read and to turn into graphs."
    }
